\import{common}
\title{The orthogonal and unitary groups in synthetic homotopy theory}
\author{trebor}
\taxon{Question}

\p{
  Define the orthogonal groups #{\mathrm{O}(n)} and the unitary groups #{\mathrm{U}(n)} in synthetic homotopy theory, together with their actions on the spheres of corresponding dimensions. Their deloopings as well as the direct limits #{\mathrm{O}}, #{\mathrm{BO}} etc. are also of interest. These definitions are necessary for the study of Bott periodicity, as well as the #{J}-homomorphism in the homotopy groups of spheres.
}

\p{
  There has been [work](https://www.davidjaz.com/Talks/DJM-Hottest-Dec-2023.pdf) on defining the tangent unit sphere bundle of spheres. It is plausible that we can build on this construction to define the orthogonal group. It is however unclear how we would define the group operation. See also [these slides](https://www.math.uwo.ca/faculty/kapulkin/seminars/hottestfiles/Christensen-2024-04-11-HoTTEST.pdf).
}
